 the slope $m$ of the line we're trying to find must satisfy\n\n$$\nm\\cdot (1)=-1\\,⇒\\,m=-1.\n$$\n\nWe know that the line passes through the point $(0,1).$ Using point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the line in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =-1(x-0) \\\\ y-1 & =-x \\\\ y & =1 -x\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535280 17592186045443 true] [17592186490397 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186175923.py" 13194139535280 17592186045443 true] [17592186490397 1169 #uuid "d4f8e14e-e664-5d3c-b8e6-ce7ab96b3db1" 13194139535280 17592186045443 true]] :edb/tempids {"2034e111-3281-5462-b0b0-a7ccb1a7c133" 17592186490394 "8d9a6db0-05c1-5d85-8a67-056821eb3220" 17592186490395 "e6fe3232-91eb-5c5b-90f0-5931f279e031" 17592186490396 "generator" 17592186490397}}
